.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt SEMGET 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm semget ,
.Nm semop ,
.Nm semtimedop ,
.Nm semctl
.Nd System V semaphores
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sem.h
.Ft int
.Fn semget "key_t key" "int nsems" "int semflg"
.Ft int
.Fn semop "int semid" "struct sembuf *sops" "size_t nsops"
.Ft int
.Fn semtimedop "int semid" "struct sembuf *sops" "size_t nsops" "const struct timespec *timeout"
.Ft int
.Fn semctl "int semid" "int semnum" "int cmd" "..."
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A set is
.Fa nsems
semaphores, each a value from 0 to 32767, 0 when the set is made.
.Fn semget
finds or makes one as
.Xr shmget 2
does a segment, from a table of 64; a count past 32000 is refused, and a
new set must have one at least.
.Pp
.Fn semop
applies the
.Fa nsops
operations at
.Fa sops ,
at most 500, at once: each an increment, a decrement that leaves no
value below 0, or, for 0, a wait until the value is 0.
While one cannot be applied, none is, and the caller waits, counted in
that semaphore's
.Dv GETNCNT
or
.Dv GETZCNT ,
unless the operation has
.Dv IPC_NOWAIT .
.Fn semtimedop
waits at most the relative
.Fa timeout .
.Dv SEM_UNDO
records the operation's opposite for the process, applied when its last
thread ends, the value kept within 0 and 32767; a child of
.Xr fork 2
has no adjustments.
.Pp
.Fn semctl
takes
.Dv GETVAL ,
.Dv GETPID ,
.Dv GETNCNT
and
.Dv GETZCNT
of semaphore
.Fa semnum ,
.Dv SETVAL ,
.Dv GETALL
and
.Dv SETALL ,
whose array the fourth argument points at, and
.Dv IPC_STAT ,
.Dv SEM_STAT ,
.Dv SEM_STAT_ANY ,
.Dv IPC_SET ,
.Dv IPC_RMID ,
.Dv IPC_INFO
and
.Dv SEM_INFO
as
.Xr shmctl 2
takes its own.
.Dv SETVAL
and
.Dv SETALL
clear every process's adjustment of what they change and wake the
waiters;
.Dv IPC_RMID
wakes them with
.Er EIDRM .
.Ss System call interface
The direct calls are numbers 393
.Pq Fn semget ,
394
.Pq Fn semctl
and 420,
.Fn semtimedop_time64 ,
whose timeout has 64-bit seconds.
i386 has no direct
.Fn semop
or 32-bit
.Fn semtimedop ;
both are
.Xr ipc 2 Ns 's.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn semget
returns an id,
.Fn semop
and
.Fn semtimedop
0, and
.Fn semctl
the value asked for, 0, or what
.Xr shmctl 2
returns for the same commands; on failure -1 with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er E2BIG
More than 500 operations.
.It Bq Er EACCES
An alteration of a set the caller may not write, or a wait on one it may
not read.
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
An operation with
.Dv IPC_NOWAIT
that would wait, or a timeout that ran out.
.It Bq Er EFBIG
A semaphore past the set's.
.It Bq Er EIDRM
The set was removed while the caller waited.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal ended the wait.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
No operations, an id with no set, a count outside what
.Fn semget
takes, or a semaphore number past the set's for
.Fn semctl .
.It Bq Er ERANGE
A value past 32767, or an adjustment past 32767 either way.
.El
.Pp
.Fn semget
and the commands it shares with
.Xr shmctl 2
fail as those do.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipc 2 ,
.Xr msgget 2 ,
.Xr shmget 2 ,
.Xr proc 5
